    "title": "Where to watch Kansas vs. Cal Baptist in the NCAA Tournament",
    "text": "March 20, 2026, 2:00 p.m. MTOf all the eight Big 12 teams that made the NCAA Tournament, none have more questions swirling around them than the Kansas Jayhawks.After a tumultuous 23-10 season, the Jayhawks find themselves as a No. 4 seed facing the WAC Champion and No. 13 seed Cal Baptist in the opening round of the tournament. All eyes will be on Kansas' Darryn Peterson in this one; the star freshman averages nearly 20 points per game and is set to be a top pick in the NBA Draft, if he chooses to declare.While Peterson draws the headlines, the Jayhawks have been without him for over a third of the season and had to lean on players like Tre White and Flory Bidunga to fill the void. Bidunga's ability to reel in rebounds will be key for the Jayhawks in clutch time, while White is a stellar 3-point shooter, making 42% of his attempts from long range.Kansas makes its money by being more physical and beating teams on the glass, with Melvin Council Jr. and Byrson Tiller providing solid support in those key areas. While Cap Baptist has the size to hang with Kansas, the physicality will be unlike much of what the Lancers have seen this season.Cal Baptist is going to lean on its star guard, Dominique Daniels Jr., who is a walking bucket. Daniels averages 23 points per game and three assists, most of which find the hands of his duo guard Martel Williams. The Lancers will need a big game out of Jonathan Griman, their 6-foot-11 forward, to help get second-chance opportunities and keep their offense alive.The winner of this game will go on to face either No. 5 Saint John's or No. 12 Northern Iowa in the second round. Here are all the details on how to watch this nightcap:Kansas basketball vs. Cal Baptist: TV channel, tip timeDate: Friday, March 20TV Channel: CBSStart Time: 8:45 p.m. CT, 7:45 p.m. MTThe Jayhawks and the Lancers will tip off at 7:45 p.m. MT from Viejas Arena in San Diego, California.Where to stream Kansas vs. Cal BaptistKansas-Cal Baptist will be available to stream on the NCAA March Madness app (with a TV provider login) and on Fubo, which offers a free trial to new subscribers.Watch Kansas vs. Cal Baptist in the NCAA Tournament on FuboContact/Follow us @BuffaloesWire on X (formerly Twitter) and like our page on Facebook for ongoing coverage of Colorado news, notes and opinions.",
